WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.770
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:07.770
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:13.070
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:13.070
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:18.450
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:18.450
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:23.740
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:23.740
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.080
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:29.080
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.340
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.340
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:39.720
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:39.720
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:45.810
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:45.810
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:51.360
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:51.360
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.440
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.440
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.740
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:00.740
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:07.020
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:07.020
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.670
namida kareru made

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:12.670
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:17.720
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:17.720
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:23.050
namida hareru made

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:23.050
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:28.060
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:28.060
though I may lose my way,

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:31.900
egakikake no ima

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:31.900
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.400
kizamu

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:39.150
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.690
akashi

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:39.150
kono te de

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.520
The surgery was a success?

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.660
Really?

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.850
Yeah, I just got the call.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:10.100
They said he'll be able to pitch next season if he does proper rehab during the off-season.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.810
That's great.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.230
Yes. Okay.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.150
Thank you so much for calling.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:18.880
Bye!

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.440
So his surgery went okay?

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.710
Yeah, apparently he was saying he wants to pitch in the television series.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.320
Television?

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.670
Oh, Division Series.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.470
Is that what it is?

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.050
He can go to the World Series if he wins that, right?

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.180
Man...

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.970
Shouldn't you at least know the basics since your boyfriend is a major leaguer?

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:48.210
The quarter-finals, played by the top three teams and the wild card team, are called the Division Series.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:52.650
The winners of those games play in the semi-finals, or League Championship Series.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:59.990
The Northern League and Southern League champions then play in the finals, or World Series.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:00.990
What?

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.110
There are still that many games?

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.490
If they don't lose.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.700
I see...

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.410
I'm sure he wishes he could pitch...

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:15.420
The Tenacity for Glory

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:15.420
The Tenacity for Glory

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.340
Safe!

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:33.350
They won.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.460
Yeah.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.530
They beat the Titans in a high-scoring game, so major props to them.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:41.290
At this rate, they might make it all the way to the World Series.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.870
Well, it can't be anything other than getting to the World Series and winning it.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.270
World Series...

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.820
I'm jealous that they're letting you out of here so soon.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.000
When did they say you can start pitching again?

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.130
If all goes well, I'll be ready before next season.

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.540
Oh, I see.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.470
That's good for you.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.230
Oh yeah, do you already know where you're going next year?

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.390
Oh...

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:17.440
All the offers were dropped.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.730
What?!

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.420
I'm just an injured veteran player now.

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:24.320
All the teams dropped their offers at the last minute,

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.160
so I'll be playing with the Hornets.

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.240
Although, I don't think it's all that bad.

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:36.630
As long as I'll be able to fight alongside you in a Hornets uniform.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.320
Sophia.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.140
I wasn't expecting the management to arrange a ride for me.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.640
I guess I'm already considered a star?

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:56.880
It's not exactly anything to celebrate about.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:03.030
H-Hey!

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.890
You're coming inside?!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.750
Hey, what do you think you're—

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:14.630
Is this everything?

00:05:14.630 --> 00:05:16.440
I'll be taking these.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:21.890
My job this time is to control Goro Shigeno.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:25.360
By that, I mean everything from rehab to diet.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:26.800
Control?

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:32.940
The management has taken the fact that you hid your injuries very seriously.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:37.990
You also lied last year in order to play in the minors.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:41.410
You worsened your yips by not informing the management of your condition.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:42.650
W-Wait a minute!

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.700
That was...

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.160
Under normal circumstances, you'd be facing heavy punishment,

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.890
or you might even be released from the team.

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:50.370
They're all cases of serious misconduct.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.740
Release?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.540
A-As in fired?!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:59.980
However, the fans and the management acknowledge your skills as a pitcher.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:03.930
The owner also thinks highly of your star potential.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.450
That's why I've been sent to keep you under control.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:15.560
It's all to keep you a part of the Hornets for as long as we can.

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.270
So that's how it is.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:25.030
Anyway, you're now prohibited from training, let alone touching a ball until the end of the year.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:29.410
I'll be cooking all three meals every day to keep you on a healthy diet program.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.980
I don't exactly like the sound of that, but I guess I don't have a choice.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:36.170
Sure thing.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.960
Well, that's how it is.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:43.710
Your spare key.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:51.140
He should have left the hospital by now.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:56.320
Eating out all the time isn't exactly good for you.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.800
I'm almost done, so go ahead and finish that vegetable soup.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:04.320
It's the top of the first, and the game has already taken an interesting turn.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:12.680
The winners of this seventh game between the Texas Raiders and Chicago Bisons will be the Southern League champions,

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:18.040
and the great Joe Gibson has taken the mound after a five-day break.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:22.960
With just one out and runners on first and second, the Raiders have created a scoring chance off Gibson.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:28.050
Batting fourth, Gibson Jr. is now making his way to the batting box.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:34.530
If the Hornets keep winning, we'll play against one of these two teams in the World Series.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:36.640
What's this?!

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:42.060
Gibson Jr. is going to bat from the left against the southpaw Gibson!

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:51.600
I've had zero hits off of you in my last sixteen at-bats against your resurrected fastballs,

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:54.030
but it'll be different today!

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:58.870
I'll hit one off you with the very strategy you taught me to beat Goro Shigeno.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.210
Out!

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.160
Out!

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:16.220
Damn, he threw a two-seam fastball.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:19.140
That was a nice play by Gibson.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.730
He knew Junior was after his fastball, so he quickly took him out.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.530
Your soup's going to get cold.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.940
Oh, okay.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:29.980
You're gonna drink it all at once?

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.950
Hey, Shigeno.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.320
Do you have a girlfriend?

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:35.660
What?!

00:08:36.020 --> 00:08:39.230
Seeing how many injuries you've had,

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:43.080
you have to completely change your diet and lifestyle.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:49.520
To do that, you need someone who'll manage your life and diet all the time.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.460
If you want to continue being a professional athlete,

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.610
I suggest you get married as soon as you can.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.070
Sh-Shut up!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.830
Like that matters!

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:00.960
Well, I'm going home.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.040
Make sure to eat the rest of your dinner in the kitchen.

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:04.980
Okay.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.060
Yes?

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:07.680
You picked up!

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.900
O-Oh, it's you, Shimizu.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.040
Th-That's all you have to say?

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.910
I've been trying to get in touch forever,

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.210
but your phone's always off.

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:19.200
Yeah, sorry about that.

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.780
You got discharged, right?

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.080
How's your injury?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.820
There's nothing to worry about.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.150
I'm doing rehab too.

00:09:26.150 --> 00:09:29.090
Oh yeah, I almost forgot, Shigeno.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.890
Make sure you get to bed early.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:34.560
I'll come cook breakfast tomorrow at eight.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.120
Okay, thanks.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:39.670
Sorry about that, Shimizu.

00:09:39.670 --> 00:09:40.990
What were you saying?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.360
Wh-Who was that woman?

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:48.100
It's night time there, right?

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.650
Why is there a woman in your room at night?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.390
Oh, it's nothing.

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:54.690
She's from the team's management.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.730
She comes to cook for me.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.430
Oh, I-I see.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.800
W-Well, cool.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:03.630
I'm glad you're doing okay.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.780
I need to go to school, so bye.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:06.660
Sure, bye—

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.220
What's with her?

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.480
I... hung up without thinking, but...

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.730
No way.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.350
Not him!

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:23.810
He...

00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:28.740
He wouldn't cheat...

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.080
Strike out!

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:43.370
A slider?

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.220
You disappoint me, Dad!

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.740
Why don't you pitch your fastballs at me?

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:51.320
Are you that afraid of giving up a hit to your son?

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:54.240
Yes, I am.

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:58.960
I'm not nice enough to throw the best batter on the team what he wants.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:03.870
The guy who started batting right handed to hit southpaws' breaking balls better

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:06.160
switched back to hitting left against a southpaw.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.050
I'd say I couldn't be any luckier.

00:11:15.390 --> 00:11:17.730
The Bisons got the first run.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:21.780
Seeing how Gibson's doing today, this'll be tough for the Raiders.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:27.830
Now hitting, number 4: Joe Gibson Jr.!

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:29.780
I was naïve.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:34.250
I thought he'd proudly throw fastballs if I faced him with my left,

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:39.670
but there's no way he'd take the bait in such an important game.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.970
Right handed batting?

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:46.890
I can't hit his breaking balls from the left.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.310
I have to do something from this side.

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:50.490
Play!

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:58.390
Strike!

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.760
Damn, I knew he'd bring out his fastballs.

00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:06.120
Strike two!

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:11.540
If I try not to swing late, he simply changes his speed.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:14.570
I must say, he's a great pitcher.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:19.160
I'm not good enough to beat him yet.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.490
Strike out!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:29.140
And he goes down with three pitches!

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:32.720
Gibson Jr. still can't hit off of his great father.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:34.270
What is he doing?

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.190
That would've been a ball.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:39.110
You're making it way too easy for him, Junior.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.030
The Bisons are leading 2-0.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.520
Gibson is the lead-off hitter in the bottom of the eighth,

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.490
but is he going to be switched out?

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:50.540
Gibson has made 95 pitches so far.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.790
Switch him out, please.

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.120
We still have a chance against a different pitcher.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.820
This is the end.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.380
We can't score two runs seeing how he's playing today.

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:06.600
Play!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.480
Hit by pitch!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:20.610
G-Gibson!

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:32.500
It was his right hand.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.710
Man, that scared me.

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:40.460
It wasn't a pitch he couldn't dodge.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.690
You'll never make it, Dad!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.980
Safe! Safe!

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:09.780
How crazy is that guy?

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:15.710
Hey, you've thrown roughly 100 pitches since the start of the game,

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:19.620
and you're recklessly sliding head first despite your two point lead?

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.550
Are you trying to get hurt for nothing?

00:14:23.560 --> 00:14:25.080
For nothing?

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.970
How is earning another run "nothing"?

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:33.280
Your soft way of thinking is why you can't get a single hit off of me.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.390
Wh-What?

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:38.480
Your last strike out made me realize something.

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:44.290
We won't lose to a team whose cleanup hitter has already given up.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:51.310
Even in my long baseball career, I've only been to the World Series four times.

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:54.160
There are many great players who couldn't even get there.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:15:00.900
Everyone dreams of that special stage and plays for their team and the champion ring,

00:15:00.900 --> 00:15:04.250
other than a certain cleanup hitter who's already given up.

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:09.880
There's very little difference in strength between the teams that have made it this far.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.180
The only difference

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:16.600
is the strength of their desire to play in the World Series!

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.200
Damn it!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.410
Safe!

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:44.370
3-0!

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.590
That's an important run for the Bisons!

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:52.220
Gibson!

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:57.810
Out!

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:03.760
Just two more outs.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:07.170
He could switch to Franco, the closer, any minute.

00:16:15.340 --> 00:16:15.910
Safe!

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:27.610
Yes!

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:28.840
One out and runners on first and third!

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:31.170
Out!

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:39.810
Please, don't get an out here.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.140
Ball.

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:49.610
Foul!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.520
Ball.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.240
Ball.

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:54.800
Foul.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:57.070
Ball.

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.160
Ball four!

00:16:58.700 --> 00:16:59.530
Yes.

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:07.560
Top of the ninth, the cleanup hitter, Gibson Jr., steps up with two outs and runners on first and second.

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:10.100
This is a big moment that could decide the series.

00:17:17.570 --> 00:17:18.350
Play!

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.780
100 mph?!

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:30.690
Are you kidding?

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:31.610
It's the ninth inning.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:38.800
You won't get a hit off of me, Junior.

00:17:38.800 --> 00:17:41.700
We will go to the World Series!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:49.790
Strike two!

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.210
The only difference

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:56.900
is the strength of their desire to play in the World Series!

00:17:58.830 --> 00:18:00.170
That's right.

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:03.970
I don't need to defeat my father.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:08.350
Foul.

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:14.150
I don't need to get a clean hit off of this amazing man.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:16.360
Foul.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.140
Ball.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:21.700
Damn.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.410
I don't care if I look like I'm struggling.

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:34.210
Gibson! Gibson! Gibson!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:37.420
Junior! Junior! Junior!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:52.730
Gibson! Gibson! Gibson!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:52.730
Junior! Junior! Junior!

00:18:55.390 --> 00:18:58.250
I have to win, no matter what,

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:04.280
and with all the Raiders' fans,

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:08.370
go to the World Series!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:36.890
It's out of here!

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:43.490
Gibson Jr. hits a game-changing three-run homer in the ninth inning!

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.140
Wow.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:20:00.300
They had such an amazing match in the very moment that decided the league title.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:02.760
Strike out!

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.180
Game over!

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:06.850
4-3!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:10.610
The Texas Raiders are going to the World Series!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:40.050
Mom, Melissa, I finally got a hit off of Dad.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:45.030
See ya.

00:20:49.460 --> 00:20:50.810
Dad!

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:53.250
Why are you here?

00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:55.850
I couldn't come here at all during the season,

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.190
so I thought I'd give my prayers.

00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:01.940
Your hand!

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:03.450
Is it from when you were hit?

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:06.490
Yeah, I fractured a bone.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:15.710
Even if it's not your pitching hand, it still must've held you back!

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:19.380
In the end, I only got a hit off of you because you were injured!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.230
Who do you think I am?

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:28.340
I'm not arrogant enough to stay on the mound if I can't pitch my best.

00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.690
You've become a great batter, Junior.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:37.190
Have some confidence.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:40.060
You did the best job a cleanup hitter could do.

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:44.740
You took the great Joe Gibson's best pitch to the back screen.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:51.180
I'm sure Mom and Melissa are both rejoicing over your growth.

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:54.440
Become a world champion.

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:03.020
Yeah.

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:16.600
Where were you going?

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.680
I hope you weren't thinking about going running.

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:21.820
Oh, I was...

00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:25.100
I'll cook breakfast, so let's get back to your room.

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:28.350
Don't do anything unnecessary.

00:22:28.350 --> 00:22:31.030
Yeah, I know.

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:33.930
Damn.

00:22:33.930 --> 00:22:36.670
Why do I have to be stuck in a place like this?

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.460
kaze to hizashi no naka de

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.460
Amid the wind and the sunlight,

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.180
hashiru anata wo miteta

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:58.180
I followed you running with my eyes.

00:22:58.390 --> 00:22:59.850
yume wo

00:22:58.390 --> 00:23:03.020
You were chasing your dream.

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:03.020
oikaketeiru

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:05.810
ground no ue ni

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:09.020
Your sweat fell on the baseball field,

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:09.020
ochiru ase ga

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.990
mabushikatta yo

00:23:09.480 --> 00:23:12.990
and it looked so dazzling.

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:20.410
wakariatteirutsumori datta

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:20.410
I thought we understood each other,

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:27.710
issho ni warai naita kara

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:27.710
because you and I both shared laughs and tears.

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:32.460
kokoro no ue ni

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:35.530
There are identical footprints on both of our hearts.

00:23:32.460 --> 00:23:35.530
onaji ashi ato

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:38.090
zutto mae kara

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:43.140
I had unconciously liked you for a long while now.

00:23:38.090 --> 00:23:39.850
kizukazu ni

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:43.140
suki ni natta

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:45.430
atsuku sugoshita

00:23:43.140 --> 00:23:50.270
My feelings were hiding in the days we spent, full of passion.

00:23:45.430 --> 00:23:50.270
tsukihi ni kakureteta

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:52.860
zutto mae kara

00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:57.950
We've been drawn to each other for so long now.

00:23:52.860 --> 00:23:54.740
otagai ni

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:57.950
hikareteita

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:00.160
kono kimochi wa

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:07.160
This feeling I have for you is what youth left behind.

00:24:00.160 --> 00:24:07.160
seishun no wasuremono

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:15.280
Preview

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:15.280
Preview

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:14.660
It's so much more unhealthy to stay put after seeing such an amazing match.

00:24:14.660 --> 00:24:16.640
Wait, why are you here?!

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:18.200
What?! Shimizu!

00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:19.910
No, y-you've got it all wrong!

00:24:19.910 --> 00:24:22.770
There's a reason deeper than the ocean itself!

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.940
Next time, on Major: To the Future.

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:27.290
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:31.000
Next Time

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:31.000
Next Time

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:31.000
To the Future

00:24:24.940 --> 00:24:31.000
To the Future
